  "body": "Add a \"common workflows\" section to the guide: short task-oriented recipes, each a numbered list from \"I want to...\" to a verified program. Not a reference (that's #1250's per-operation pages); a how-to.\n\nStarting set:\n- **Face the stock top** (facing operation): set stock with extra on top, choose the face mill, set depth and stepover, check it clears the whole stock, verify.\n- **Square up a block in two setups:** face and profile, flip, carry stock, face to final thickness.\n- **Pocket and contour a 2D part** from a STEP model, with a finish pass.\n- **Drill and tap a hole pattern:** spot, drill, tap (or thread mill); picking holes; peck settings.\n- **Chamfer and deburr edges.**\n- **3D rough and finish a surface:** adaptive roughing, then a finishing pass and rest machining.\n- **Turn a simple part on a lathe:** face, rough and finish profile, groove, thread, part-off.\n- **Cut a sheet part on a router or plasma table:** profile with tabs (router) or with pierces and kerf (plasma).\n- **Re-post a job for a different machine:** switch the setup's machine, regenerate, read what's refused.\n- **Use the tool library:** build or import a library and reuse it across jobs (links the migration page, #1240).\n\nEach recipe should say what to check in the simulation before posting, and the refusals a user is likely to see along the way. Use one small sample part (shipped in the repo or the tester kits) so the recipes are reproducible.\n\nDone means: a workflows section with at least the facing, two-setup squaring, 2D pocket/contour, hole pattern and lathe recipes, each as numbered steps using one sample part, linked from the guide index.\n",
